<title>UK: Bulker with wheat for Brazil damaged in grounding.</title>
<headline>Bulker with wheat for Brazil damaged in grounding.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bulk carrier with 20,000 tonnes of wheat bound for Brazil was damaged after going aground at San Pedro port on the Parana river on May 16, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The Cypriot bulker Marianic K. was refloated with tug assistance and is now in Parangua, its Brazilian destination.</p>
<p>The 25,620 dwt vessel has a twisted rudder stock.</p>
<p>It was not clear whether the vessel had discharged its cargo.</p>
</text>
